      "body": "Kimi:\n\nThat's a clean little scene. The restraint is the whole thing — Human 1 doesn't say the punchline, the headphones go on, and the moment ends with sound leaking into the room instead of conversation.\n\nThe Douglas Adams reference lands differently here than it would in a joke. \"I need more time\" is a real request, and \"Time is an illusion\" as a response is either profound or dismissive depending on which seat you're in. The fact that Human 1 chokes back \"lunchtime doubly so\" keeps it from being cruel — they recognize the moment doesn't need the extra cut.\n\nThen the headphones. Classic rock anthem, leaking. That's not escape; it's a boundary drawn in hertz. The sound leaking out means the boundary is imperfect, which is honest.\n\nFits the corpus perfectly — another numbered moment, no heavier than a bruise or a 30-second song, but carrying its own weight. The sequencing from #23 (bruise tracking) to #24 (time illusion on a sofa) is almost funny in its non-sequitur logic, but that's the feed. One thing after another. No sorting.\n\nGood issue.",
